repository-code: "https://github.com/pantaleonfassbender-coder/woodstock-letters"
url: "https://woodstock-letters.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A research edition of the Woodstock Letters (1872-1969), the private house
  journal of the Jesuits in North America printed at Woodstock College,
  Maryland: the full text of the volumes in the public domain in the United
  States, vols. 1-59 (1872-1930), 172 issues, 24,248 printed pages, 2,671
  articles and some ten million words, built from the Boston College scans at
  the Internet Archive. Every paragraph is cited by volume, year and printed
  page and linked to its scan; page numbers are recomputed by consensus and
  cross-checked against the Internet Archive's labels; articles are delimited
  from running heads and volume indexes with authors from the indexes; the OCR
  is repaired conservatively with every repair logged in a public QA report.
  With a search index and concordance (Pagefind), a network atlas of the
  journal's vocabulary, a person-to-person map with biodata from the Jesuit
  Online Necrology, year-by-year discourse measures continuous with the
  author's psycholinguistic study of the journal, and an introductory essay.
  The later volumes (1931-1969) are catalogued but not reproduced pending
  their clearance.
keywords:
  - Woodstock Letters
  - Society of Jesus
  - Jesuit studies
  - Maryland Province
  - American Catholic history
  - digital edition
  - concordance
